  abstract={Breast cancer is still the very communal and fatal diseases that women throughout the globe suffer from. Timely and accurate finding through medical imaging especially ultrasound is crucial for suitable treatment planning and prognosis. However, manual ultrasound image evaluation is prone to variability and diagnostic errors. This research implements an automatic deep learning-based method for categorizing ultrasound images of breast into benign, malignant, and normal classes. This research paper used a public dataset with over 1500 ultrasound images in three diagnostic classes. The CNN abstracts the spatial structures, the LSTM seizures the temporal dependencies and this implementation built an optimized hybrid CNN-LSTM model. The model was trained by employing data augmentation and transfer learning with the deep learning neural-net architecture to increase robustness and accuracy. Training accuracy 93.6% and validation accuracy 86.7% was obtained. The validation loss is low and thus well developed. High classification accuracy was corroborated using visualization techniques such as confusion matrices and prediction overlays particularly for malignant cases. Augmentation was further applied to correct a class imbalance issue that allowed the model to perform well. The optimized fusion of CNN - LSTM model is promising its performance to support radiologists in cancer recognition by considering the ultrasound images and can serve as an effective and scalable clinical decision-support solution.},
