  abstract={This study proposes an effective end-to-end system in the area of predictive analytics in the healthcare industry, and the two major goals of the system are to predict the treatment outcome and the expected treatment duration. An enhanced version of the machine learning pipeline is used in the backend to generate informative features such as risk scores, clinician efficiency, and hospital capacity to boost the prediction results. To achieve accurate classification results, the pipeline addresses the issue of class imbalance using the SMOTE algorithm and feature selection to utilize the most impactful features in the model. A set of machine learning models such as XGBoost, CatBoost, and Random Forest are used to achieve the goals of the system and are optimized to achieve accurate results in classification and regression problems. A user-friendly Streamlit-based interface is provided to the end-users to obtain accurate predictions based on interactive parameters related to the patients and the hospitals. Accurate results such as the predicted outcome, treatment duration, and prediction confidence are provided to the end-users, along with the essential analytical tools such as the top features and model performance metrics (Accuracy, MAE, RMSE).},
