  pages={1469-1476},
  abstract={The most life threatening disease is cancer that affect humanity together with Lung Cancer (LC) severity detection followed by timely treatment remains the most effective way to reduce mortality. Among various kind of mortality disease, LC has placed second prevalent disease after heart disease that can be often diagnosed during advanced stage which results in poor survival outcomes. Although complete prevention of LC is not feasible, LC severity detection can significantly improve treatment effectiveness along with patient survival rates. Conventional diagnostic approaches rely on multiple laboratory tests and medical imaging. However, these methods are often limited by delayed diagnosis together with variability in interpretation. Hence, in addressing these challenges, several data analysis using Machine Learning (ML) together with Deep Learning (DL) approaches had introduced for LC severity detection, yet issues related to accuracy, robustness, and reliable severity identification persist to better treatment. The maingoal of this study is to enhance the accuracy and efficiency of benign LC detection by developing a precise classification framework for multiple lung disease target classes. The proposed approach employs a Convolutional Autoencoder (CAE) as a transfer learning (TL)–based feature extraction model to obtain high-level along with discriminative features while minimizing data redundancy. These optimized features are subsequently passed to a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) technique in capturing the sequential along with contextual dependencies for effective classification. However, evaluating experimental results have demonstrated the proposed CAE–LSTM framework achieves a classification accuracy of 96.50% and exhibits superior generalization performance comparing with conventional methods. Thus, the findings mentioned that the proposed hybrid DL model can serve as a reliable decision support tool for LC severity detection along with assist clinicians in improving diagnostic outcomes.},
